{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Yitzhak sowed in that land.</b> As the blessed El had told him: <b>Dwell in this land.</b>" "<b>A hundredfold.</b> As He had promised in saying: <b>And I will be with you and bless you.</b>" "<b>And YHWH blessed him.</b> With wealth, for he sold his produce at high prices. And according to what the Sages of blessed memory said — that this man's estimate was for tithes (Genesis Rabbah 64:6) — He established for him a blessing for their sake, as it says: הָבִיאוּ אֶת הַמַּעֲשֵׂר אֶל בֵּית הָאוֹצָר וַהֲרִיקֹתִי לָכֶם בְּרָכָה עַד בְּלִי דָי (Malachi 3:10)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {2 "Genesis Rabbah 64:6 is cited as סד:ו; this is the standard chapter-verse form for Genesis Rabbah, here referring to the midrash on Genesis 26:12."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:48.463483777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}